# channel_injector.cron.example
#
# Sample crontab entry for tools/channel_injector.  Copy-paste into
# the crontab of the same user that runs the meshcore-watchlist
# daemon (so the venv is reachable and ownership of any log file is
# consistent).  Edit the URL(s) and schedule to taste.
#
# Install:
#     crontab -e          # as the meshcore-watchlist run-user
# Or system-wide:
#     sudo install -m 0644 \
#         install_script/channel_injector.cron.example \
#         /etc/cron.d/meshcore-watchlist-channel-injector
#     # Then prepend "USER " before the schedule on each line for
#     # /etc/cron.d/ — see crontab(5) on your distro.
#
# Notes
# -----
# * Use the FULL PATH to the venv's python.  cron has a minimal
#   environment and there is no shell activation; a bare "python"
#   may resolve to the wrong interpreter or none at all.
# * The "cd" puts the install dir on sys.path so the
#   "tools.channel_injector" package import resolves.
# * --source-url may be repeated to merge multiple upstream lists.
# * Stdout + stderr are appended to a logfile so cron's mail-on-
#   output behaviour stays quiet on success.

# Every 15 minutes, sync the upstream channel list.
*/15 * * * * cd /opt/meshcore-watchlist && /opt/meshcore-watchlist/.venv/bin/python -m tools.channel_injector --source-url https://example.org/channels.json >> /var/log/channel_injector.log 2>&1

# Example with two upstream sources and INFO logging:
# */30 * * * * cd /opt/meshcore-watchlist && /opt/meshcore-watchlist/.venv/bin/python -m tools.channel_injector -v --source-url https://example.org/channels.json --source-url https://other.example/list.json >> /var/log/channel_injector.log 2>&1
